# Title: Forfiles.EXE Child Process Masquerading
# ID: f53714ec-5077-420e-ad20-907ff9bb2958
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), Anish Bogati
# Date: 2024-01-05
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1036
# Description: Detects the execution of "forfiles" from a non-default location, in order to potentially spawn a custom "cmd.exe" from the current working directory.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((process.parent.command_line:*.exe OR process.parent.command_line:*.exe\") AND process.executable:*\\cmd.exe AND process.command_line:/c echo \"*) AND NOT (((process.parent.executable:*:\\Windows\\System32\\* OR process.parent.executable:*:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\*) AND process.parent.executable:*\\forfiles.exe AND (process.executable:*:\\Windows\\System32\\* OR process.executable:*:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\*) AND process.executable:*\\cmd.exe)))
